# UI and Styling

- Use the global palette in `app/globals.css` only
	- ink `#010203` (`bg-ink`, `text-ink`)
	- surface `#1D1D1F` (`bg-surface`)
	- stone `#3B3130` (`border-stone`, `border-line`)
	- gold `#B16C04` (`text-gold`, `bg-gold`)
	- highlight `#D3AC2C` (`text-highlight`, `bg-highlight`)
	- orange `#E87812` (`text-orange`, `bg-orange`) — primary CTA accent
	- white `#F7F4EF` (`text-white`) — high-contrast body on dark heroes
- Semantic aliases: `background` = ink, `foreground` = highlight,
	`muted`/`accent` map to gold/highlight, `line` = stone
- Do not introduce new hex colors; compose with these tokens
- Buttons: `bg-orange text-ink` (or `bg-highlight text-ink`)
- Style with Tailwind CSS (utility-first)
- Mobile-first responsive layouts
- Meet WCAG contrast: gold/highlight on ink; never stone as body text
- Consistent spacing; theme colors live as CSS variables

```tsx
<button
	type="button"
	className="rounded-md bg-highlight px-4 py-2 text-ink"
>
	Save
</button>
```
